@startuml deployment
title Local stack - docker compose

skinparam shadowing false

actor Client

node "docker compose network" {
  node "individuals-api\nhost 8081 -> 8081" as API
  node "keycloak\nhost 8080 -> 8080" as KC
  database "keycloak-postgres\nhost 5433 -> 5432" as KCDB
  database "person-postgres\nhost 5434 -> 5432" as PSDB
  node "prometheus\nhost 9090 -> 9090" as PROM
  node "tempo\nhost 3200, 4318" as TEMPO
  node "grafana\nhost 3000 -> 3000" as GRAF
}

node "person-service\n8082 - arrives in module 2" as PS

Client --> API : POST /v1/auth/...
API --> KC : Admin REST API\nand OIDC token endpoint
API ..> PS : HTTP, not running yet
KC --> KCDB : JDBC
PROM --> API : scrape /actuator/prometheus
API --> TEMPO : OTLP push /v1/traces
GRAF --> PROM
GRAF --> TEMPO

note right of PROM
  Prometheus pulls, the application pushes.
  That is why the app address lives in
  prometheus.yml while the Tempo address
  lives in application.yml.
end note

note bottom of PSDB
  Runs in module 1 only so the Flyway
  migrations have something to apply to.
  Nothing connects to it yet.
end note

@enduml
